    "created_at": "2016-05-31T19:06:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-31T19:06:22Z",
    "body": "I mean, yes, whenever you render a link, you could resolve its URL lazily. With appropriate caching that seems like a totally reasonable strategy. It's certainly a reasonable model for the spec.\n\nI don't think there are any real-world custom element use cases here.\n",
